{"org":"elastic","repo":"elasticsearch","prNumber":"111475","commit":"a18846c3a374cc8f6c18bf9cab43a4d807de4d66","generatedCommentsNodes":[{"comment":"The change from using an `AttributeMap` (which effectively acted as a set) to an `ArrayList` for collecting resolved attributes from groupings removes deduplication. If the same attribute appears multiple times within the groupings, it will now be passed as duplicates to `NamedExpressions.mergeOutputAttributes`, which may lead to duplicate attributes in the resulting plan.","nodes":[{"id":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/analysis/Analyzer.java-x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/analysis/Analyzer.java-22539:22575,22595:22607,22608:22618,22635:22647,22848:22873,23000:23034-22413:22516,22536:22545,22546:22555,22572:22581,22782:22801,22928:22936","promptId":"#0X6BJ","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/analysis/Analyzer.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/analysis/Analyzer.java","srcChanges":[{"pos":22539,"endPos":22575,"startLine":461,"startLineOffset":16,"endLine":461,"endLineOffset":52,"length":37},{"pos":22595,"endPos":22607,"startLine":462,"startLineOffset":16,"endLine":462,"endLineOffset":28,"length":13},{"pos":22608,"endPos":22618,"startLine":462,"startLineOffset":29,"endLine":462,"endLineOffset":39,"length":11},{"pos":22635,"endPos":22647,"startLine":462,"startLineOffset":56,"endLine":462,"endLineOffset":68,"length":13},{"pos":22848,"endPos":22873,"startLine":466,"startLineOffset":24,"endLine":466,"endLineOffset":49,"length":26},{"pos":23000,"endPos":23034,"startLine":469,"startLineOffset":86,"endLine":469,"endLineOffset":120,"length":35}],"dstChanges":[{"pos":22413,"endPos":22516,"startLine":459,"startLineOffset":16,"endLine":459,"endLineOffset":119,"length":104},{"pos":22536,"endPos":22545,"startLine":460,"startLineOffset":16,"endLine":460,"endLineOffset":25,"length":10},{"pos":22546,"endPos":22555,"startLine":460,"startLineOffset":26,"endLine":460,"endLineOffset":35,"length":10},{"pos":22572,"endPos":22581,"startLine":460,"startLineOffset":52,"endLine":460,"endLineOffset":61,"length":10},{"pos":22782,"endPos":22801,"startLine":464,"startLineOffset":24,"endLine":464,"endLineOffset":43,"length":20},{"pos":22928,"endPos":22936,"startLine":467,"startLineOffset":86,"endLine":467,"endLineOffset":94,"length":9}]}]},{"comment":"Changing the return type from `UnsupportedAttribute` to `UnresolvedAttribute` is inconsistent with other changes in this chapter (e.g., #SS25M), which move towards using `UnsupportedAttribute` for known fields that cannot be used due to specific constraints. This semantic shift may result in less descriptive error messages for the user, as \"unresolved\" typically implies a lookup failure rather than a type incompatibility or unsupported operation.","nodes":[{"id":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/analysis/Analyzer.java-x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/analysis/Analyzer.java-52208:52228,52334:52413-52110:52129,52174:52178","promptId":"#8PJ1J","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/analysis/Analyzer.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/analysis/Analyzer.java","srcChanges":[{"pos":52208,"endPos":52228,"startLine":1070,"startLineOffset":27,"endLine":1070,"endLineOffset":47,"length":21},{"pos":52334,"endPos":52413,"startLine":1073,"startLineOffset":20,"endLine":1073,"endLineOffset":99,"length":80}],"dstChanges":[{"pos":52110,"endPos":52129,"startLine":1068,"startLineOffset":27,"endLine":1068,"endLineOffset":46,"length":20},{"pos":52174,"endPos":52178,"startLine":1068,"startLineOffset":91,"endLine":1068,"endLineOffset":95,"length":5}]}]}],"groundTruthGeneratedCommentsNodes":[{"groundTruth":{"original_line":461,"line":461,"comment_lines":["[461][]"],"review_comment":["I think it\u0027s important we use something that tracks the order of attributes, because this is used below in `mergeOutputAttributes`. Using the `AttributeMap` could lead to funky errors in case of attribute shadowing in the groupings.","The role of AttributeMap is to guarantee equality - while it can deal with ordering (it\u0027s a linkedmap), it\u0027s better to have this recorded elsewhere such as a list.","Ah, fair point; however, there shouldn\u0027t be groupings with same name id but different names, so the `mergeOutputAttributes` below should take care of deduplicating fine.\r\n\r\nI think using the `AttributeMap` here is less obvious (I completely forgot the thing preserves iteration order), esp. since an `AttributeSet` seems to suffice."],"path":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/analysis/Analyzer.java","id":37259,"created_at":"2024-08-06T12:50:02Z","original_position":21,"side":"LEFT","position":29,"submitted_on_commit":"a18846c3a374cc8f6c18bf9cab43a4d807de4d66","diff_hunk":"@@ -458,17 +456,17 @@ private LogicalPlan resolveStats(Stats stats, List\u003cAttribute\u003e childrenOutput) {\n                 }\n             }\n \n-            if (stats.expressionsResolved() \u003d\u003d false) {\n-                AttributeMap\u003cExpression\u003e resolved \u003d new AttributeMap\u003c\u003e();","submitted_line":462},"generatedCommentsNodes":[{"comment":"The change from using an `AttributeMap` (which effectively acted as a set) to an `ArrayList` for collecting resolved attributes from groupings removes deduplication. If the same attribute appears multiple times within the groupings, it will now be passed as duplicates to `NamedExpressions.mergeOutputAttributes`, which may lead to duplicate attributes in the resulting plan.","nodes":[{"id":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/analysis/Analyzer.java-x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/analysis/Analyzer.java-22539:22575,22595:22607,22608:22618,22635:22647,22848:22